# Local environment files — NEVER commit these
#
# ⚠️  WARNING — READ BEFORE CREATING ANY NEW .env FILE ⚠️
# The patterns below only cover `.env.local` and `.env.<name>.local`.
# A plain `.env` is NOT ignored: create `apps/backend/.env` with a real database
# password or JWT key and the next `git add -A` will commit it, permanently, into
# history (git keeps deleted blobs — see POLICY-SEC-001).
#
# Rules:
#   1. Real secrets go in `.env.local` (ignored) — never in `.env`.
#   2. `.env` is for non-secret, build-time values only, and only where the
#      values are public by nature. The one tracked `.env` in this repo,
#      `apps/admin/.env`, holds a localhost API URL and an app title: Vite bakes
#      every VITE_* var into the shipped browser bundle, so nothing secret can
#      ever live there regardless of git.
#   3. Placeholders belong in `.env.example` (tracked) — never real values.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# JWT keys and secrets — NEVER commit these
secrets/
*.pem

# Firebase Credentials & Configs — NEVER commit these
firebase-service-account*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
*.p8
*.p12

# ── Flutter build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pubspec.lock is intentionally TRACKED (application repo, not a library)
apps/mobile/build/
apps/mobile/.dart_tool/
apps/mobile/.flutter-plugins
apps/mobile/.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Android local properties (contains machine-specific SDK paths)
apps/mobile/android/local.properties

# ── Admin React app build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/admin/dist/
apps/admin/.vite/

# ── Error and debug logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
error.log

# ── Archive bundles (generated delivery zips — not source) ─────────────────────
*.zip
